Prajāpati was the overlord.
With three they praised;
the sacred word was created;
Brahmaṇaspati was the overlord.
With five they praised;
beings were created;
the Lord of Beings was the overlord.
With seven they praised;
the seven seers were created;
Dhātṛ was the overlord.
With nine they praised;
the fathers were created;
Aditi was the overlady.
With eleven they praised;
the seasonal [periods] were created;
the seasons were the overlords.
With thirteen they praised;
the months were created;
the year was the overlord.
With fifteen they praised;
the royal power was created;
Indra was the overlord.
With seventeen they praised;
cattle were created;
Bṛhaspati was the overlord.
With nineteen they praised;
the Śūdra and the Ārya were created;
day and night were the overladies.
With twenty-one they praised;
solid-hoofed cattle were created;
Varuṇa was the overlord.
With twenty-three they praised;
small cattle were created;
Pūṣan was the overlord.
With twenty-five they praised;
wild animals were created;
Vāyu was the overlord.
With twenty-seven they praised;
heaven and earth separated;
the Vasus and Rudras came along after them;
they alone were the overlords.
With twenty-nine they praised;
trees were created;
Soma was the overlord.
With thirty-one they praised;
creatures were created;
the dark and bright fortnights were the overlords.
With thirty-three they praised;
beings found rest;
Prajāpati the Supreme was the overlord.

17.6.m:
O Agni, thrust away our born rivals; repel the unborn, O Jātavedas;
speak in our favor, favorably minded, without anger; may we be in your three-armored shelter when rising up.
With might thrust away our born rivals; repel the unborn, O Jātavedas;
speak in our favor, being well disposed; may we prosper; thrust away our rivals.
The forty-fourfold is the stoma;
splendor is the wealth.
The sixteenfold is the stoma;
might is the wealth.
You are the loose earth of the earth, named apnas; may all the gods praise you as such.
Rest here, backed by stomas, rich in ghee; sacrifice wealth for us, accompanied by offspring.
